{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 2, :comments ["<b>ha-pa'am ha-ḥamishit [the fifth time]</b> She will teach me. The vav reverts to 'my mother'." "<b>ha-pa'am ha-geshishit [the third time]</b> I will lead you, I will bring you to my mother's house, she will teach me. [My mother's house is Jerusalem, and the sense of 'she will teach me'] is that she will teach me the commandments, and I will rejoice with you as a woman who drinks wine with her husband."], :book :song-of-songs, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 8, :notes {1 "Inserted bracketed clarification around 'she will teach me' mirrors the bracket in the Hebrew source; the bracketed material appears to be Ibn Ezra's editorial clarification of the referent."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra's commentary on the Canticles" "http://beta.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH002030344/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:45:00.395738404Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}